\n" [:option {:value "159400"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159415"} "Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159427"} "Eights, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159436"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159456"} "Lightweight Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "159471"} "Single Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159486"} "Double Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159498"} "Quadruple Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159507"} "Coxless Pairs, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159519"} "Eights, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "159527"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031206"} "1896"] "\n" [:option {:value "157529"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "157643"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "157679"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "157752"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "157889"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "157941"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "158011"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "158130"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "158247"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "158322"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "158403"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "158482"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "158562"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "158659"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "158793"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "158914"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "159028"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "159183"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "159563"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159743"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "260980"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319027"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353953"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19008433"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012433"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/379"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Double Sculls, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "21 – 27 July 1996"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/718"} "Lake Sidney Lanier, Gainesville, Georgia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/159368"} "39 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "France, Norway, and Germany had won 11 of the last 12 World Championship medals and were represented at the 1996 Summer Olympics by " [:a {:href "/athletes/36996"} "Frédéric Kowal"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36850"} "Samuel Barathay"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/39150"} "Kjetil Undset"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39137"} "Steffen Størseth"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37921"} "Sebastian Mayer"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37945"} "Roland Opfer"] " respectively. France, represented in part by Barathay, was the 1993 World Champion and 1994 bronze medalist. Norway was the 1994 World Champion and 1993 runner-up and, with its Olympic duo, the 1995 bronze medalist, while Undset was also an Olympic silver medalist from the 1992 quadruple sculls. Germany had been runner-up at the last two editions of the World Championships and a bronze medalist in 1993. The lone exception to the dominance of these three nations was Denmark, who won the 1995 World Championships with " [:a {:href "/athletes/36479"} "Lars Christensen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36502"} "Martin Haldbo Hansen"] ". Australia, meanwhile, sent one of its defending Olympic champions, " [:a {:href "/athletes/35347"} "Peter Antonie"] ", to Atlanta with a new partner, " [:a {:href "/athletes/35384"} "Jason Day"] ". Antoine was also one half of the winning crew at the 1995 Double Challenge Sculls at the Henley Royal Regatta. Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/38126"} "Zsolt Dani"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38171"} "Gábor Mitring"] " were the 1994 winners of that tournament."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the opening round, Norway posted the fastest time by nearly five seconds, while the other heats were won by Denmark and the Italian duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/38512"} "Davide Tizzano"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38264"} "Agostino Abbagnale"] ", both of whom were Olympic champions in the quadruple sculls from 1988. The Hungarians, meanwhile, were eliminated in the repêchage. In the semi-finals it was France who eliminated the Australians with the fastest time in the round, nearly three seconds ahead of its closest competition, while Italy won the other heat. The race in the final was closer, but Italy, Norway, and France were all ahead of the pack and crossed the finish line in that order. Denmark, the reigning World Champions, came in fourth nearly five seconds later."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/38512"} "Davide Tizzano"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/38264"} "Agostino Abbagnale"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/39150"} "Kjetil Undset"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/39137"} "Steffen Størseth"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/36996"} "Frédéric Kowal"] " / " [:a {:href "/ath